### 7 Platform, infrastructure and operations
- [ ] **(Eng)** **The backend runs on Vercel serverless functions** (seen in the deployed logs: `/var/task`). A function is frozen once it answers and killed after its time limit, so nothing long-running works there: the automation view server and test runs (now refused with a clear 501), the deal watcher (reminders, stall alerts), the approval timeout watcher, the escrow / QC / freight pollers, the 15-minute IMAP poll, the daily digest, durable NATS consumers and the long-lived approvals stream (SSE). Move the backend to a long-running host (VM, Render, Railway, Fly, Docker) — or keep the API on Vercel and run the background jobs and automation on a separate long-running worker.
- [ ] **(Eng)** Durable event bus (NATS) — 1.5.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Background watchers have no lock.** The deal watcher, escrow watcher, HITL timeout watcher, QC / freight / escrow pollers and the digest run in every process. Two backend replicas would send every reminder twice and sweep twice. Add a leader lock (Mongo lease) or run them in one worker. — done 2026-11-18: `shared/leader_lock.py` — each tick of the deal / escrow / HITL timeout / stale-negotiation watchers, the digest and the trade-min scheduled jobs takes a Mongo lease (`watcher_locks`); one instance acts, another takes over when the lease runs out; without Mongo every instance runs; an unreachable store skips the tick (`LEADER_LOCK_FAIL_OPEN`).
- [ ] **(Eng)** Backups: Mongo Atlas continuous backup with point-in-time restore; a restore drill; Google Drive document folder backed up.
- [ ] **(Eng)** Monitoring and alerting: error rate, webhook failures, stuck deals, open exceptions, money gate age, provider error rates, LLM failure rate; alerts to Telegram / e-mail; on-call owner. — progress 2026-11-18: real-time Telegram alerts for stalled watchers, the leader-lock store, LLM failure rate per caller, refused webhooks, money gates pending over `MONEY_GATE_ALERT_HOURS` (24) and exceptions piling up (`OPEN_EXCEPTIONS_ALERT` 10). Error-rate / provider-error dashboards and an on-call owner: still open.
- [ ] **(Eng)** Deployment: decide the monolith (`app.py`) vs per-service containers for production, health checks, rolling deploy, zero-downtime migrations.

