### 14.1 Legal entity — Starting the company (non-technical: registrations, accounts, set-up)
- [ ] **(Biz/Legal)** Choose the legal form: private limited company (recommended: escrow providers, banks and foreign buyers expect it, and it limits personal liability), LLP or proprietorship. Decide before anything else — every registration below is in the entity's name.
- [ ] **(Biz/Legal)** Class 3 digital signature certificates (DSC) for every director / partner — needed for incorporation, DGFT (IEC), GST, ICEGATE and income-tax filings.
- [ ] **(Legal)** Incorporate on the MCA portal (SPICe+): name approval (check the "PortLess" name and trademark are free first), DIN for directors, MoA / AoA, Certificate of Incorporation with CIN; the company's PAN and TAN are issued with it.
- [ ] **(Biz)** Registered office: a real address with proof (rent / lease agreement, owner's NOC, recent utility bill). GST officers may visit; this address goes on every document (`PORTLESS_ADDRESS`).

### 14.2 Tax and trade registrations — Starting the company (non-technical: registrations, accounts, set-up)
- [ ] **(Legal)** GST registration (GSTIN) for the principal place of business — needed for every export, the LUT and refunds (also 3.1).
- [ ] **(Legal)** IEC (Importer-Exporter Code) from DGFT, linked to the company PAN (also 3.1). **Update it on the DGFT portal every year (April – June) or it is deactivated.**
- [ ] **(Legal)** GST LUT (letter of undertaking, form RFD-11) for the current financial year — export without paying IGST; renew every April (also 3.1).
- [ ] **(Legal/Ops)** ICEGATE registration and the bank's AD code registered with customs at each port of export (also 3.1).
- [ ] **(Legal)** Registration-cum-Membership Certificate (RCMC) from the export promotion body for each product traded: **Spices Board CRES for spices (HS 0904 pepper / chilli, used in testing — mandatory for spice exporters)**, **APEDA for basmati and other agri products** (basmati contracts also registered with APEDA, see 3.1), FIEO for products with no specific council.

### 14.3 Bank and payment accounts — Starting the company (non-technical: registrations, accounts, set-up)
- [ ] **(Biz)** Current account in the company's name with an **AD Category-I bank** (one that handles foreign exchange), with internet banking, SWIFT details for the PI, and an **EEFC account** to hold export proceeds in USD. EDPMS reporting of every shipping bill runs through this bank (also 3.1, 3.2).
- [ ] **(Biz)** Business (KYB) accounts with Tazapay, Escrow.com and the supplier payout route (also 1.1, 3.3). They ask for the incorporation certificate, PAN, GST, IEC, director KYC, the website and a description of the business — finish 14.1 – 14.4 first.

### 14.4 Brand, website and contact details — Starting the company (non-technical: registrations, accounts, set-up)
- [ ] **(Biz/Ops)** Domain name and business e-mail on it (trade desk, accounts, inspections), with SPF / DKIM / DMARC (also 1.3).
- [ ] **(Biz/Ops)** Company website: who PortLess is, products and markets, how an order works (escrow stages, third-party inspection), registered address, CIN / IEC / GSTIN, contact, privacy policy and terms. Escrow providers, banks and buyers check it, and it must match the details given at KYB.

### 14.5 Advisers and service providers — Starting the company (non-technical: registrations, accounts, set-up)
- [ ] **(Biz)** Chartered accountant on retainer: GST returns and refunds, LUT, books, tax.
- [ ] **(Biz/Ops)** Licensed customs broker (CHA) under contract at the ports used — files the shipping bill until ICEGATE filing works (also 1.2, 5.2).

### 22.2 Review-board findings (2026-11-18) — P0
- [x] **(Eng) P0** **A supplier's directory usual price or an ex-works price counts as a firm FOB quote on the match board** — Give SupplierOffer a price basis (quoted / usual / estimate, FOB / EXW); only a written quote is "quoted"; EXW gets the inland leg (as the standby list already does) before any margin; a usual price makes the pair an estimate until the RFQ reply. Why: no deal is confirmed on a margin that disappears when the supplier quotes for real. Evidence: shared/orchestration/matchmaking.py:270-272 — any offer with fob_price_usd_per_mt gets basis "quoted"; supply_first.py stores the directory's usual price (source directory_usual_price) and manual_suppliers converts an EXW price without adding the road to the port. (review-board B-01 2026-11-18) — done 2026-11-18: `SupplierOffer.price_basis` (quoted / usual / estimate) + `incoterm` + `port_km`; `trade_costs.exw_to_fob` adds the road to the port before any margin; a usual or estimated price makes the pair an estimate (sigma 6 %, missing "supplier's written quote"); manual suppliers store the FOB equivalent; supply-first offers are `usual`, RFQ quotes `quoted`.
- [x] **(Eng) P0** **Hand-made and supply-first deals never get the deal-created checks** — Run the deal-created leg (enrichment, compliance.check_trade, outreach, RFQ) on every move into MATCHING — or emit DEAL_CREATED with status MATCHING from update_status / supply_first. Why: a prohibited product or an embargoed buyer is stopped before PortLess spends on outreach — or ships it. Evidence: shared/orchestration/continuations.py:712 — on_deal_created only acts on DEAL_CREATED with status MATCHING; a deal created without an opportunity starts DRAFT (services/deals/service.py:529) and later moves to MATCHING by PATCH /deals/{id}/status or supply_first.start, which never emits it again. (review-board B-02 2026-11-18) — done 2026-11-18: `deals.update_status` DRAFT → MATCHING emits `DEAL_CREATED` (status MATCHING, `entered_matching`), so hand-made and supply-first deals get enrichment, compliance, outreach and the RFQ; other moves into MATCHING emit nothing.

