### 4 Money safety and financial controls
- [x] **(Eng)** Export the double-entry journal to the accounting system (Tally / Zoho Books / your CA's format) — CSV exists (`/escrow-guard/journals`); add account codes agreed with the CA. — done 2026-11-18: `?format=tally` / `?format=zoho` on `/escrow-guard/deals/{id}/journal` and `/journals` (one debit and one credit row per entry; ledger names from `JOURNAL_LEDGER_<ACCOUNT>`). Confirm the layouts with the CA's software on a real import.
- [x] **(Eng)** FX: record the rate at each receipt and payout and post FX gain / loss to the journal (today amounts are USD only). — done 2026-11-18: `shared/orchestration/fx_book.py` + `POST/GET /escrow-guard/deals/{id}/fx` (staff: PO rate, payout and receipt bank rates); the journal posts the gain / loss of each INR payout against the PO rate to `fx_gain_loss`; deal page card.
- [x] **(Eng)** Fees: reconcile the escrow provider fee, payout fee and bank charges per deal against the fee % assumed in the cost sheet; alert when actual > assumed. — done 2026-11-18: `shared/orchestration/fee_check.py` — staff record actual fees from statements (`POST /escrow-guard/deals/{id}/fees`: escrow / payout / bank); compared with the % priced in (cost sheet / `PAYOUT_FEE_PCT`; an unassumed fee is over at any amount); `GET …/fees`, `GET /escrow-guard/fees/over`, digest line "FEES ABOVE THE PRICE".
- [ ] **(Biz)** Kill Switch drill: pause, confirm every money path refuses, resume — monthly.
- [x] **(Eng)** Alert when realised margin on a closed deal is below the margin floor (cost sheet estimate vs actual costs). — done 2026-11-18: when every tranche is released and the supplier is paid in full, a realised margin below the deal's margin floor (else `DEALMAKER_PO_MARGIN_FLOOR_PCT`) raises `deal.exception` `PAID:margin_below_floor` (category MARGIN_BREACH) once, with the estimate, net received, supplier paid and PortLess's costs; mid-deal figures are never judged.
- [x] **(Eng)** Supplier retention (10 % held until buyer acceptance): confirm the supplier contract states it, and the payout e-mail explains it. — payout e-mail done 2026-11-18: the payment notice says how much is held until the buyer accepts (its share of the order value), why, and that it is paid on acceptance or when the window lapses (`retained_until_acceptance` on `payout.completed`). The supplier contract wording is still for counsel (3.4).
- [x] **(Eng/Legal) P1** **Cargo insurance from the supplier's warehouse to the buyer's place, per Incoterm** — the cost sheet has one marine-insurance % (`marine_insurance`, CIF only). PortLess is the exporter, so it carries the risk from the supplier's warehouse until the risk passes under the term. (1) Inland transit cover from the supplier's warehouse to the port for every term, FOB / FCA included (the e-way-bill truck). (2) The sea leg for CIF / CIP, insured by PortLess to the named port / place at 110 % of the CIF value, with the buyer as the party paid: Institute Cargo Clauses (C) for CIF, (A) for CIP. (3) D-terms (DAP / DPU / DDP) insured to the buyer's door. (4) FOB / CFR / CPT: seller's-interest (contingency) cover in case the buyer's own cover does not respond. Cost-sheet lines per segment (`insurance_inland`, `insurance_marine`, `insurance_contingency`); the per-shipment declaration under the open policy made before the ship sails, with its certificate number on the CI and the insurance declaration (with the 3.5 Ops item); the warehouse-to-warehouse transit clause on the certificate. A claims step tied to a dispute: survey at destination, notice within the policy's days, claim against the insurer and the carrier, recovery booked in the journal. — done 2026-11-19: `shared/orchestration/cargo_insurance.py`: cost-sheet lines per leg once the buyer's term is known (`insurance_inland` on EXW / FCA supply, `marine_insurance` at 110 % with ICC (C) / (A) for CIF / CIP / D-terms, `insurance_contingency` for F- / C-terms); declaration certificate number on the CI and insurance declaration (`POST /deals/{id}/insurance/declaration`); claims opened → notified → surveyed → filed → settled / rejected with the notice deadline (`INSURANCE_CLAIM_NOTICE_DAYS`) and recovery in run costs. Journal posting of a recovery stays open.

### 5.1 Found in the automation runs (open) — Workflow gaps found end to end
