- [ ] **(Eng/QA)** Standby supplier switch (UC-13 / UC-14): a standby supplier from a scan has only a town, so its inspection now waits for an address — re-run both journeys and confirm the request goes to the new supplier.
- [x] **(Eng)** Cross-prospect offers: the match board pairs a buyer with supplier offers from other deals of the same HS code, including old ones. Confirm `MATCH_OFFER_VALIDITY_DAYS` expiry is enough, and never propose an offer from a CANCELLED / failed deal without a fresh price. — done 2026-11-18: the match board never takes an offer from a CANCELLED / REFUNDED / PAID / failed deal (already), and now also skips the supplier of a QC_FAILED / DISPUTE deal, offers whose check failed, quotes whose reconfirmation lapsed and do-not-contact suppliers.
- [x] **(Eng)** Negotiation drafts still sometimes say things like "As soon as we have the inspector selected, we will send the proforma invoice" — review a sample of real drafts each week (stage wording, missing-information order). — done 2026-11-19: drafts that put the order steps in the wrong order (PI waiting for the inspector / inspection, PO before the escrow, inspection before funding) are flagged `stage_order_wrong`, held at L0 with the reason on the approval (`stage_order_errors`, tests/test_stage_order_wording.py). A weekly read of real drafts stays an Ops habit.

