- [x] **(Eng/Ops) P1** **Customs house agent (CHA / licensed customs broker) hand-off per shipment** — ICEGATE filing is a stub and `POST /shield-link/deals/{id}/customs/manual` only records the result; the steps before it are not in the system. (1) A CHA list per port (`cha_agents`: firm, customs broker licence number under CBLR 2018 and its validity, ports, contact, charges per shipment / per container; seeded from A.40) with one chosen per lane. (2) The CHA's KYC of PortLess kept once (IEC, GSTIN, PAN, AD code, LUT, signed authorisation letter — CBLR 2018 reg. 10) and re-sent when one changes. (3) At QC_PASSED the CHA gets the pack by e-mail with a `[CHA:<deal>]` token: CI, PL, SDF, Shipping Bill checklist, the inspector's loading record, e-way bill, certificates, and which incentives to claim. Its checklist reply waits for staff approval (new gate `APPROVE_SB_CHECKLIST`, L0), and only then may it file. (4) The Shipping Bill number, date, port code, LEO date and the RoDTEP / RoSCTL / drawback declarations it carried are read from the CHA's reply or entered by staff; they feed realisation and incentive credits. (5) The CHA's invoice (agency, CFS, THC, examination) is recorded against the cost-sheet line `cha`, with an overrun alert like freight (`cost_overrun.py`). Tests on recorded e-mails. — done 2026-11-19: `shared/orchestration/cha.py`: CHA list per port with licence validity (`PUT /deals/cha/agents`), KYC record + what is missing / changed, pack e-mailed at QC_PASSED with a `[CHA:<deal>]` token and the incentives to declare, the checklist reply opens `APPROVE_SB_CHECKLIST` (L0; APPROVE tells the CHA to file), Shipping Bill number / date / port / LEO / declarations read from the reply or staff (`INCENTIVE:not_declared`), CHA invoice vs the cost sheet (`CHA:cost_overrun`). Seeding the list from A.40 waits for the actor.
- [x] **(Eng/Ops) P1** **Empty container survey before stuffing** — the inspector's loading record has container and seal numbers, but nothing says the box was fit for food. Before stuffing, the inspector (or a container surveyor) checks each empty box: valid CSC plate, no holes or light, dry, clean, odour-free, no previous-cargo residue or nails, doors and gaskets intact, liner / kraft paper / desiccant where the packing spec asks, and for reefer cargo the pre-trip inspection (PTI) and set temperature. Record per box `container_survey` (passed / rejected, defects, photos, surveyor) through the QC webhook loading fields or `POST /shield-link/deals/{id}/loading`. A rejected box asks the carrier for a replacement (Maersk booking amendment) and stuffing waits. The compliance shipment check refuses T2 and `BOOK_FREIGHT` while a stuffed box has no passed survey (`container_survey_missing`). The QIMA loading-supervision booking and the SGS / BV request name the survey, and the survey report joins the buyer's documents and the evidence pack. — done 2026-11-19: `LoadingRecord.container_surveys` per box (QC webhook or `POST /shield-link/deals/{id}/loading`); `CONTAINER_SURVEY_REQUIRED` → shipment finding `shipment_container_survey` (block) until every stuffed box passed; a rejected box raises `CONTAINER:rejected` (ask the carrier for a replacement); QIMA booking and the portal request name the survey. The Maersk booking amendment for a replacement box is still done by staff.

### 5.3 Process design to confirm with the trade desk — Workflow gaps found end to end
- [ ] **(Ops)** Who approves which gate, response-time targets per gate, and the backup approver when the first is away (L1 timeouts default: negotiation e-mails 4 h → approve, money 24 h → reject).
- [ ] **(Ops)** What happens on a QC FAIL at the second attempt (playbook cancels / refunds — confirm the business rule and supplier penalty).
- [ ] **(Ops)** Demurrage / detention: who pays when the buyer clears late; nothing tracks it today.
- [ ] **(Ops)** Quality claims after delivery beyond the acceptance window (warranty period, evidence, partial refund) — only full dispute / refund exists.
- [x] **(Eng/Ops)** **Samples before the first order.** Buyers of agri commodities usually ask for a sample before they commit; nothing in the flow handles it (the word "sample" in the code is only QIMA's sampling level). Add a sample step on the prospect: buyer asks (read from the reply) → sample requested from the supplier → courier AWB recorded (DHL / FedEx / India Post; a sample is not an export shipment, but courier rules and the destination's food-import rules still apply) → buyer's verdict. Cost per sample on the deal's run costs, and an approved sample becomes the quality reference written into the PI / PO and the QC booking ("as per approved sample ref …"). Found 2026-11-19 (export-business video, stage 6). — done 2026-11-19: `shared/orchestration/samples.py`: request read from the buyer's reply or staff, courier + AWB + cost (run costs `samples_usd`), verdict; the approved sample is the quality reference in the PI / PO description and the QC note (`/deals/{id}/samples`).
- [x] **(Eng/Ops) P1** **Letter of intent (LOI) from a buyer — and the LOI / ICPO / FCO broker-chain pattern** — many buyers send an LOI before a PI; nothing reads one or asks for one. (1) An LOI template PortLess can send a new buyer on a large lot: product + spec, quantity and tolerance, price range, Incoterm® 2020 + named place, delivery window, payment through escrow, validity, non-binding except confidentiality. (2) A buyer's LOI (body or PDF attachment) is read into the `BuyerRequirement` (firm quantity, window, port, spec) with `commitment=loi`; the match board raises the chance of closing for it, and the PI quotes the LOI reference. (3) A guard: the classic commodity-scam chain from intermediaries ("LOI → ICPO → FCO → SPA → POF / BCL", "SGS at load port", "buyer's mandate", "procedures") is flagged `broker_chain_pattern`, forces L0, and is never answered with bank details, proof of funds or company documents. An LOI counts only from a buyer that is screened and writes from its own domain. — done 2026-11-19: `shared/orchestration/loi.py`: an LOI read from an interested buyer's reply (or `POST /deals/{id}/loi`) onto the deal and the candidate's requirement (`commitment=loi`, match-board chance ×1.15), the PortLess LOI template (`GET /deals/{id}/loi/template`), and the broker-chain guard: two or more ICPO / FCO / SPA / POF / BCL / mandate / procedure markers → the e-mail is held at L0 (`broker_chain_pattern`). Printing the LOI reference on the PI stays open.

