### 17.1 National trade statistics next to Comtrade — Trade data beyond UN Comtrade
- [x] **(Eng)** **UK HMRC trade data connector** (free API, uktradeinfo.com OData; monthly imports by CN8 code and partner, value **and kg**): fills the UK lines where Comtrade has a value but no quantity, so no unit price and no gap (14 UK buyers dropped as "no measured price gap" on 2026-11-17). Direct connector, no Apify cost; Phase 1 source for market `GB`. — done 2026-11-19: `uk_hmrc` (`shared/connectors/national_trade.py`, OData OTS, GBP → USD with the reference rate) in Phase 1 for GB: live demand from the monthly quantity and the buyer anchor when the actor has none. Field names from the public docs — verify on live data.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Eurostat Comext connector** (free API; monthly EU imports by CN8 code, partner and quantity in 100 kg): fresher than Comtrade's annual figures and 8-digit (grade-level) codes for DE, ES, NL, FR, IT … Direct connector; Phase 1 source for EU markets. — done 2026-11-19: `eurostat_comext` (JSON-stat, EU27 reporter, partner India + extra-EU, EUR → USD) in Phase 1 for EU markets, same use as HMRC. Verify on live data.
- [x] **(Eng)** **US Census** — already a connector: turn it on with the free `CENSUS_API_KEY` (owner track A) and give it the US monthly import price per HS10 as the buyer anchor when fresher than Comtrade. — done 2026-11-19: Census now returns monthly value and kg (US and India unit value per MT) and joins the merge rule as a national source when fresher than Comtrade; needs the free `CENSUS_API_KEY`.
- [ ] **(Eng)** **India's own export statistics — PortLess side** (needs actor A.1, section "Apify actors"): connector slot + normaliser, then use it for (1) what each market pays for INDIA's goods this year (the radar's `india_to_market` anchor, today Comtrade, often two years old); (2) a supplier-side check (India's FOB per destination); (3) whether India already ships the product to the market; (4) the trend per destination. Tests on recorded rows.
- [ ] **(Eng)** **Mirror data for markets that report late or not at all** (UAE, other Gulf states, many African markets): use partners' exports to the market (Comtrade mirror flows; the export-market actor already returns a `mirror` flag) and India's exports to it (actor above) when the market's own import figures are missing or older than two years. UAE data on 2026-11-17 is from 2023 and shows prices below India's average (negative gaps, 23 UAE buyers dropped).
- [ ] **(Eng)** **Investigate UAE / Dubai customs open data** (Dubai Pulse / Federal Competitiveness and Statistics Centre) as a direct source for the UAE; an Apify actor only if there is no API.
- [x] **(Eng)** **One merge rule for every source**: per product × market take the freshest source with a quantity (HMRC / Comext / Census monthly → TradeStat → Comtrade annual → mirror), record which one on the opportunity (`price_benchmark_source`, `data_period`), and show the source and month on the radar. A source that disagrees by more than 30 % with another is flagged, not averaged. — done 2026-11-19: Phase 1 takes the freshest figure with a quantity (national monthly vs actor annual, `_period_key`), records `price_benchmark_source` + `data_period`, flags `sources_disagree` beyond `SOURCE_DISAGREE_PCT` (25).
- [x] **(Eng)** **8-digit codes end to end**: the national sources speak CN8 / HS10 / ITC-HS8; map them to the catalogue's product lines (15.1 "exact product code") so a price is per grade, not per 6-digit mix — fixes many "price check needed" gaps. — done 2026-11-19: the catalogue's `hs8_codes` go to UK HMRC (exact CommodityId) and Eurostat (product = CN8), so their price is per grade.
- [x] **(Eng)** Demand gate uses these sources too: a market with recent monthly imports from a national source is "live demand" even when Comtrade has nothing (89 buyers were dropped as "no live demand data" on 2026-11-17). — done 2026-11-19: recent monthly imports from UK HMRC / Eurostat count as an active Phase 1 source (done with the connectors, 2026-11-19).
- [ ] **(QA)** Tests per connector on recorded responses (`httpx.MockTransport`), the merge rule (freshest-with-quantity wins, disagreement flagged), and the actor's normaliser; readiness shows each source live / stub.
- [ ] **(Eng/Biz) P1** **ITC Trade Map (trademap.org) as a source** — ITC's free database (registration; free for users in developing countries such as India) has monthly / quarterly data for many reporters, mirror data, unit values per partner, India's competitors per market and lists of importing companies by product and country. There is no public API, so first read its terms of use. If automated reading is allowed, use actor A.39; otherwise staff import Trade Map's Excel / CSV exports (`POST /trade-min/trade-map/import`). Either way the data goes into the price book, the merge rule (a source with its `data_period`) and the directory (importers as buyer candidates, source `trade_map`).


### 18.1 Opportunities from companies, not only from market statistics — How opportunities are found
- [x] **(Eng)** **Company-led opportunities**: group the buyer / supplier directory by product × country; where at least `COMPANY_LED_MIN_BUYERS` (3) checked buyers with a usable e-mail and at least 2 reachable suppliers exist, create an opportunity even without a Comtrade gap. Price it from the price book / mandi / any market price, mark it "no market statistics" (`source=directory`), and let the profit ranking and the ready-to-start checklist judge it like any other. On 2026-11-17 the UAE had 42 named importers and no opportunity; 232 of 287 directory buyers were linked to none. — done 2026-11-19: `GET / POST /trade-min/opportunities/company-led`: ≥ `COMPANY_LED_MIN_BUYERS` verified contactable buyers + ≥ 2 reachable suppliers per product × country → an opportunity priced from the price book, `found_by=directory`, same pair matching / start check / profit.
- [ ] **(Eng)** **Profit gate instead of the gap gate**: today a corridor without a measured Comtrade gap builds no opportunity (`_scan_one`: "no live demand data" / "no measured price gap" dropped 126 buyers on 2026-11-17). Keep a corridor whenever buyer price (any source) − supplier price (any source) − landed costs clears the margin floor; the Comtrade gap becomes one input and a warning (`price_check_needed`, `no_market_statistics`), never the gate. Never invent a price: no price on one side still means no opportunity, listed in the scan report with what is missing.
- [x] **(Eng)** **The worldwide search adds markets**: a country where the worldwide buyer search (`_worldwide_counterparties`, 53 companies on 2026-11-17, "not tied to a scanned market") found at least N buyers of a product is proposed as a new market for that catalogue line (staff accept with one click on the Catalogue page) and scanned next time, instead of the companies staying in the directory only. — done 2026-11-19: `GET /trade-min/catalogue/proposed-markets` (≥ `WORLDWIDE_MARKET_MIN_BUYERS` contactable buyers of a product in a country not yet in the line) and `POST …/accept` adds it for the next scan.
- [ ] **(Eng)** **Demand signals create opportunities**: a buyer's inbound reply or enquiry (e-mail mapped to no deal), an RFQ or tender, a buyer who asked for another product during outreach, and a past buyer due to reorder (11.4 "repeat orders") each create or refresh an opportunity for that product × market with the buyer attached first — the strongest demand there is, today none of them can start one.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Supplier-led opportunities**: a checked Indian supplier with a price and capacity for a product (scan, RFQ reply, manual supplier 5.5) is matched against every market whose directory buyers want the product, not only the scanned corridors; surplus capacity offered by a supplier starts a search for buyers (links 5.5 "supply-first deal"). — done 2026-11-19: `GET /trade-min/suppliers/{id}/markets`: every market whose contactable directory buyers want the supplier's products, ranked; `…/start-prospect` starts one.
- [x] **(Eng/Ops)** **Clean the roles in the directory**: run the quality check (`quality.py`) over the stored directory — "buyers" in India for export markets and companies flagged `role_suspect` become suppliers (when they make the product) or are dropped from outreach; today the check only runs on new scans (30 Indian "buyers" on 2026-11-17). — done 2026-11-19: `POST /trade-min/directory/clean` now also runs `directory.clean_roles()`: an Indian `role_suspect` "buyer" that makes / ships the product becomes a supplier record (`moved_from_buyer`), the rest stay out of outreach; staff-held records are never moved.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Radar shows how each opportunity was found**: source chip "market statistics" / "directory" / "buyer enquiry" / "supplier offer" / "worldwide search", filter by it, and count per source in the scan report — so the operator can compare which source turns into deals (feeds 11.4 funnel analytics). — done 2026-11-19: `EnrichedOpportunity.found_by` (market_statistics / national_statistics / …), `GET /trade-min/opportunities?found_by=` and `/opportunities/found-by` counts. The other chips arrive with company-led / enquiry opportunities (18.1).
- [ ] **(QA)** Tests: company-led opportunity from 3 checked buyers + 2 suppliers without Comtrade; profit gate keeps a corridor with no gap but a clearing margin and drops one with a price missing (scan report says what); a proposed market from the worldwide search; an inbound enquiry creates an opportunity; Indian "buyer" re-roled; browser case for the source chip and filter.
- [x] **(Eng/Ops) P1** **Buyer enquiries from government portals and Indian missions abroad** (source: export-trainer reel, 2026-11-19) — free, government-backed buyer leads that PortLess does not use yet. (1) **Trade Connect and the Indian Business Portal**: enquiries reach the trade mailbox (owner track C). The Email Processor recognises them by sender / subject and reads product, HS, quantity, country and the buyer's contact into a buyer candidate with its `BuyerRequirement` (source `trade_connect` / `indian_business_portal`). They go through the normal check (screening, e-mail, `role_suspect`) before any outreach. A matching open prospect gets the candidate, otherwise the lead becomes a demand signal (the item above). (2) **Indian embassies / consulates (commercial wing)**: per preferred market, a templated request from the trade desk — product, HS code, quantity range, PortLess's profile, IEC / RCMC — asking for a list of importers. The commercial wing's address goes in the country profile (`commercial_wing_email`). Each request is tracked (market, HS, sent, reply, list received; a reminder after 14 days, at most one request per market × HS a quarter). A returned list (e-mail body, Excel or PDF) is imported into the directory as buyers (source `indian_mission:<cc>`, staff confirm the import) and then checked like any scanned buyer. (3) The scan report and the radar's source chip show these sources, and the funnel counts how many of their leads reach PI. Trade Map's company lists, also named in the reel, are already the 17.1 item and A.39. — done 2026-11-19: `shared/orchestration/gov_leads.py` + `demand_leads.py`: Trade Connect / Indian Business Portal enquiries recognised in the Email Processor, read into a lead → directory buyer (stated quantity) + candidate on a matching prospect; mission requests per market × HS (`POST /deals/missions/requests`, `commercial_wing_email` on the country profile, one a quarter, reminder after `MISSION_REMINDER_DAYS`), `[MISSION:<id>]` replies parsed and imported once staff confirm; `GET /deals/leads/stats` counts leads and PIs per source. Registering on the portals is the owner-track item.


### 19.1 Prospect desk — trading the prospect stage
- [x] **(Eng)** **Prospect desk** — done 2026-11-17 (`shared/orchestration/prospect_desk.py`, `GET /deals/prospects/desk`, Prospects page): per prospect the best buyer × supplier pair (margin/MT, chance, expected value, firm or estimate), the radar's original estimate, whose move it is (`us` / `buyers` / `buyer` / `suppliers`) and for how many days, stalled (idle ≥ `PROSPECT_STALL_DAYS` 5), quotes expiring / expired, undelivered introductions, and ranked next moves (confirm, send offer, push supplier, best and final, reconfirm quote, contact buyers, chase quotes, fix mailbox, park after `PROSPECT_DROP_DAYS` 21, drop). Summary cards: pipeline value, ready to confirm, our move, stalled, quotes to reconfirm; sort by priority / value / idle / newest; filter "Our move" / "Stalled".
- [x] **(Eng)** **Walk-away and target prices per pair** — done 2026-11-17 (`matchmaking.negotiation_targets`): highest supplier FOB and lowest buyer price that keep the margin floor, and both at the target margin (`MATCH_TARGET_MARGIN_PCT` 12); "push the supplier to ≤ X FOB (−Y/MT) or the buyer to ≥ Z" as the next step when under the floor; match board column "Walk-away".
- [x] **(Eng)** **Quotes: age, validity, leverage** — done 2026-11-17: quote age and days of validity left per pair, "expires in N days — ask to reconfirm" within 3 days, expired quotes listed on the board (still not scored), best quote and spread with "ask the other suppliers to match or beat it".
- [x] **(Eng)** **One cost model for radar and match board** — done 2026-11-17: the board uses the radar's lane freight (`freight_lanes`), reefer per product and confirmed export incentives (`incentives`), shown in its assumptions.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Outreach e-mail fixes found on live data** — done 2026-11-17: (1) the contact finder's note to the operator ("Write to einkauf@… — the purchasing inbox … (MX ok, listed on /kontakt/)") was the first line of every buyer introduction — now filtered (`outreach.usable_pitch`, also at scan time), the standard opener is used instead; (2) a send that fails in transport ("Connection lost") is recorded on the candidate (`send_error`, attempts) instead of leaving it "pending" as if untouched; (3) the introduction named five inspectors while only QIMA is booked — it now names only `QC_PROVIDERS_ENABLED`.
- [ ] **(Eng/Ops) P0** **Outbound mail is failing**: on 2026-11-17 every buyer introduction of the 8 live prospects failed with "Connection lost" (10 `RESOLVE_EXCEPTION` gates pending, `CALLBACK_FAILED`); no buyer has been contacted, one prospect is 7 days old. Fix the SMTP / gateway connection (1.3), then resend from each prospect (Contact next buyers) — the candidates from before the fix carry no `send_error`, so check them by hand.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Retry transport failures automatically**: a failed outreach / RFQ send retries with back-off (e.g. 5 min, 30 min, 2 h) before it becomes a `deal.exception`, and the prospect shows "Retry sends" for the operator. — done 2026-11-18: `shared/orchestration/send_retry.py` — introductions and RFQ e-mails that failed in transport are re-sent at 5 min, 30 min, 2 h (`SEND_RETRY_MINUTES`), then `deal.exception` `OUTREACH:send_failed` / `RFQ:send_failed` once; logged-only sends are not retried. `POST /deals/{id}/retry-sends` + "Retry sends" on the prospect. Fixed on the way: an RFQ e-mail that failed in transport was recorded as a portal success, and a later successful send never cleared the candidate's send error.
- [x] **(Ops/Eng)** Clean the stored operator notes out of `buyer_candidates[].pitch_angle` / directory records (the filter stops them reaching a buyer; the data still holds them). — done 2026-11-19: `directory.scrub_notes()` (run by `POST /trade-min/directory/clean`, `notes_scrubbed`) drops operator notes stored as a company's description; candidates' pitch angles were already filtered on read.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Best-and-final round by e-mail**: today the desk only suggests it. A templated e-mail to every other quoted supplier ("our best price is X FOB for this quantity — can you match or beat it by <date>?", never naming the competitor) on the RFQ thread, behind a gate; replies flow into the normal quote intake. — done 2026-11-18: `shared/orchestration/best_and_final.py`, `POST /deals/{id}/match/best-and-final` → `SEND_BEST_AND_FINAL` gate (L0); APPROVE e-mails every other quoted supplier on its RFQ thread (match or beat USD X/MT FOB by a date; the competitor is never named); replies go through the normal quote intake. Button on the match board.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Reconfirm a quote before it expires**: the deal watcher e-mails the supplier N days before `validity_days` runs out while the prospect is open ("please confirm your price of X stands until …"); a reply extends the quote, silence marks it expired. — done 2026-11-18: `shared/orchestration/quote_reconfirm.py` — `QUOTE_RECONFIRM_DAYS_BEFORE` (3) days before a quote's validity ends the supplier is asked on its RFQ thread; "we confirm the price stands" restarts the validity, a new price is a new quote, silence marks the offer `reconfirm_status=expired`.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Price discovery across buyers**: send the indicative offer to every interested buyer at once (each its own range from its own pair), keep the best reaction, and sell to the highest — today one buyer at a time. — done 2026-11-19: with a firm match proposed, the other interested buyers still get their own indicative range (`PRICE_DISCOVERY_ALL_BUYERS`); the board's expected-value order picks the best buyer and the runner-up is reported.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Counter-offer ladder**: when a buyer counters, show the concession steps from our ask to the walk-away price (in 2–3 moves) so the operator never concedes past the floor in one go; reuse `agents/negotiation_agent/pricing.py`. — done 2026-11-18: `pricing.concession_ladder` (50 / 30 / 20 % of the gap, never below the walk-away price) and `GET /deals/{id}/concession-ladder` from the negotiation (supplier's own price + every cost + margin floor); card on the deal's Negotiation tab.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Park / drop as actions**: "Park" (stop reminders, keep the record) and "Drop" (close as NEGOTIATION_FAILED / CANCELLED with a reason feeding `outcomes`) buttons on the desk, with the reason recorded — today they are suggestions only. — done 2026-11-18: `POST /deals/{id}/prospect/park` (reason, optional until-date; no follow-ups, no stall exception, listed last on the desk), `/unpark`, `/drop` (CANCELLED with the reason in the status history and outcomes; its pending prospect gates close as superseded; new transition DRAFT / MATCHING → CANCELLED). Buttons on the Prospects page.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Desk in the daily digest and Telegram**: the "our move" list and stalled prospects with their next move each morning (`shared/orchestration/digest.py`). — done 2026-11-18: the digest (Telegram + e-mail) has PROSPECTS: open / our move / stalled, the top 8 where the move is ours (best first) and the stalled ones waiting on them, each with its next move.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Effort per prospect**: e-mails sent, replies, Apify cost (16 scan cost) and operator touches next to its expected value, so prospects that eat time without moving show up. — done 2026-11-18: the desk counts e-mails sent, replies, decisions a person made and the scan cost per prospect; past `PROSPECT_EFFORT_HIGH` (12) with no interested buyer and no quote it is flagged "busy, not moving" with park / drop as the first move. Shown on the Prospects page.
