### 23.1 Existing Apify actors — changes on the PortLess side (review 2026-11-19)

What `shared/connectors/apify.py` and its callers do with the actors already in use today; each item names the actor. The actor-side changes are A.19 – A.28 in "Apify actors".

- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Daily run budget lives in process memory** — `APIFY_MAX_RUNS_PER_DAY` is counted in `_runs_by_day` (shared/connectors/apify.py), so every instance and every restart starts again at 0 and the cap can be passed several times over on a deployed backend. Count runs (and `usageTotalUsd`) in Mongo per UTC day (the `platform_costs` day document of `shared/cost_meter.py`) and check the cap there before each run of any actor. Saves: Apify overspend. — done 2026-11-19: runs reserved atomically in the `platform_costs` day document (`apify_runs`, `apify_by_actor.<key>`) before each run, undone when over the cap or when Apify refuses the start; memory only without Mongo (`shared/connectors/apify_usage.py`).
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Daily USD cap, not only a run count** — runs of `company-contact-finder-ai` (search mode, 3 lines × 5 sites) cost far more than one `email-list-qualifier-ai` run; add `APIFY_MAX_USD_PER_DAY` checked against the day's `usageTotalUsd`, with the digest showing spend vs cap per actor. — done 2026-11-19: `APIFY_MAX_USD_PER_DAY` checked against the day's `apify_usd` (each run's `usageTotalUsd`); digest shows spend vs cap and runs / USD per actor; `GET /health/costs` → `apify_budget.by_actor`.
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Result cache per actor input** — identical calls are only coalesced while in flight; the same search line ("rice importers, AE" for two rice corridors) or the same company re-checked by `counterparty-check-ai` in the next scan is paid again. Mongo cache keyed by actor + normalised input line with a TTL per actor (`company-contact-finder-ai` search 14 days, `counterparty-check-ai` = `TRADE_MIN_VALIDATION_MAX_AGE_DAYS`, `export-market-finder-ai` 30 days), hit rate on `GET /trade-min/sources`. — done 2026-11-19: Mongo `apify_result_cache` (memory without Mongo) keyed by actor + normalised input; TTL contact finder / search 14 d, screening = `TRADE_MIN_VALIDATION_MAX_AGE_DAYS`, export markets 30 d, qualifier 7 d, tracking never; `APIFY_CACHE_HOURS_<KEY>`; only SUCCEEDED runs; hits / misses / hit rate per source on `GET /trade-min/sources`.
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Scan-time screening ignores the VAT number the search already found** — `company-contact-finder-ai` returns `vat_id` (and the legal name), but the scan-time check (`services/trade_min/validation.py` → `counterparty-check-ai`) sends only name + country, so the EU VIES check (`checkVat`) never runs at scan time and a name-only sanctions match is weaker. Pass `vat_number`, `lei`, legal name and (after A.19) the register number from the directory record, as enrichment already does. — done 2026-11-19: `vat_number` / `legal_name` carried from the search onto the buyer / supplier / directory record and sent with LEI and CIN to `counterparty-check-ai`; LEI, VIES answer and VAT kept on the check (`validation.lei` / `vat_valid`).
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Carrier tracking polls a refused actor** — the deal watcher calls `multi-carrier-tracking-ai` for every forwarder-booked IN_TRANSIT deal every `TRACKING_POLL_HOURS`, and each run ends `source_refused` (the `rich_minds` plan cannot run the public carrier Store Actors): a paid run for nothing. After the first `source_refused` of the day stop polling until A.27 is deployed, and say so on the deal ("tracking: staff milestones only"). — done 2026-11-19: after the first `source_refused` of a UTC day no more tracking runs that day (`APIFY_CARRIER_TRACKING_RETRY_REFUSED=true` once A.27 runs); the deal shows `freight_status_detail` "tracking: staff milestones only".
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **A missing `email-list-qualifier-ai` row is read as "invalid"** — the actor only returns qualified rows, so a timed-out or partly failed run marks good addresses undeliverable and the company drops out of outreach. Until A.23: when the run did not end SUCCEEDED or returned fewer rows than it was asked before its own timeout, mark the missing addresses `unchecked`, not `invalid`. — done 2026-11-19: a run that did not end SUCCEEDED (or was cut at the row limit, or refused by the budget) marks the missing addresses `unchecked`, not `invalid`.
- [x] **(Eng) P2** **One paid e-mail check, not two** — `company-contact-finder-ai` already verifies the mailbox when asked (`verifyMailbox`); after A.22 ask it for the top N companies of a scan and skip `email-list-qualifier-ai` for addresses it checked. — done 2026-11-19: `COMPANY_SEARCH_VERIFY_MAILBOX` asks the company search to check mailboxes; the per-address results (`mailboxes`, A.22) set the best address's status (`mailbox_status`), so the scan-time check skips `email-list-qualifier-ai` for it.
- [x] **(Eng) P2** **Use the legal-notice facts (after A.19)** — register court + number, VAT id and managing director from the buyer's Impressum: evidence for `verified` (a registered company, not only a working mailbox), company age for `COMPLIANCE_MIN_COMPANY_AGE_YEARS`, and the related-party check (same director or address as the supplier). — done 2026-11-19: `legal_notice` normalised from the contact finder onto BuyerSignal / SellerCandidate / the directory; VAT id and register number go to the screening (`registrationNumber` for A.25), the register shows in `existence` and `register_ref`.
- [x] **(Eng) P2** **Monthly market data (after A.26)** — call `export-market-finder-ai` with monthly frequency, keep `data_period` per figure, and let the radar prefer the last 12 months over the annual figure. — done 2026-11-19: `EXPORT_MARKET_MONTHLY` sends `frequency: M` (12 months); `monthly` / `last_12m` / `data_period` / per-origin `origins` read; the market's unit value uses the last 12 months over the annual figure.
- [x] **(Eng) P2** **Retire the dormant actor slots** — `apify_us_importers` (`us-importer-finder-ai`), `apify_alibaba_rfq` (`alibaba-rfq-leads-ai`) and `apify_india_suppliers` (`india-supplier-finder-ai`, never built) are registered, never called and listed as "not used" on `GET /trade-min/sources`; remove them (or point them at A.2 / A.16 / A.10 when those are built) so the sources page shows only what can run. — done 2026-11-19: `us-importer-finder-ai`, `alibaba-rfq-leads-ai`, `india-supplier-finder-ai` removed from the connector registry and the sources page; classes kept as `apify.DORMANT_CONNECTORS` for A.2 / A.16 / A.10.

### 23.2 Agents that decide on their own — more profit per deal (review 2026-11-19)

Today two parts use an LLM: the negotiation agent (words; price decided by code) and the exception resolver. The agents below follow the same rule: **code decides every price, quantity and money step; the LLM reads and writes; every agent action goes through a gate at its autonomy level (`autonomy_policy`), is recorded in `outcomes` so its own track record can raise or lower that level, and stays inside a budget.** Ranked by money at stake.

- [ ] **(Eng) P1** **Freight procurement agent** — most forwarders and NVOCCs quote by e-mail, not API. For each deal after the PO: e-mail 3–5 forwarders on the lane (directory role `forwarder`, `[FRT:<deal>]` thread) with the container plan, ports and ready date; read the quotes (rate per box, free days, validity, transit, sailing) into `freight_lanes`; counter the best one toward the lane index / second-best quote within a code-set band; propose the booking that is cheapest for the ready date (`BOOK_FREIGHT` gate with the comparison). Profit: freight is the largest PortLess cost on CIF deals; every quote also improves the radar's lane rates.
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Inbound question agent (buyer / supplier questions answered, not parked)** — a reply that is a question (specification, certificates, packing, payment steps, inspection, lead time) goes to `NEEDS_OPERATOR` today and waits for a person. Draft the answer from the deal facts, catalogue, company profile and knowledge memory (only true statements — `company_profile` rules, `true_claims` checks), send behind `SEND_NEGOTIATION_EMAIL` (L1 4 h → APPROVE once its approval rate is high). Profit: replies within minutes instead of a day; buyers go cold when a question waits. — done 2026-11-19: `shared/orchestration/question_agent.py`: a verified question with no price on known topics is answered from the deal facts only (spec, certificates, packing, payment steps, inspection, lead time, samples) behind `SEND_NEGOTIATION_EMAIL` (flag `question_answer`); price talk / claims still go to a person.
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Supplier sourcing agent (stalled RFQs)** — when a prospect has an interested buyer but no usable quote after `PROSPECT_STALL_DAYS`, widen the supplier search on its own: other states / mandis, the worldwide and local-language search, directory suppliers of neighbouring HS codes, manual suppliers; contact-check them and send RFQs within the Apify budget, chase non-responders once, report what it tried on the desk. Profit: fewer prospects lost for want of a supplier price. — done 2026-11-19: `shared/orchestration/sourcing_agent.py`: interested buyer, no quote after `PROSPECT_STALL_DAYS` → up to `SOURCING_AGENT_MAX_NEW` unasked directory suppliers of the heading (traded → verified → manual first) get the RFQ gate; deal watcher + `POST /deals/{id}/sourcing/widen`. Other states / mandi traders wait for new list actors.
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Reorder / account agent** — the reorder module only reminds staff. Before a buyer's usual next order (`reorders.due`), price a repeat offer from current supplier quotes and the price book (code: band, margin floor, validity), write it in the buyer's thread (`SEND_INDICATIVE_OFFER` gate), and on a yes open the reorder deal with the same supplier (or the standby if it re-quoted up). Profit: repeat orders need no outreach and close at a higher rate. — done 2026-11-19: `reorder_agent.py`: before a buyer's usual next order, opens the repeat prospect, prices the range by code (last price ± supplier move, never below the minimum offer) and opens a SEND_INDICATIVE_OFFER gate on the buyer's thread; deal watcher + `POST /deals/reorders/{id}/offer`.
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Claims and dispute agent** — after a failed QC or a buyer complaint, negotiate the resolution with both sides on their own threads: options computed by code (re-inspection, discount within the margin left after the supplier chargeback, replacement lot, partial refund) and ranked by what each costs PortLess; the agent explains, asks for evidence (photos, lab report), and proposes the option behind `RESOLVE_EXCEPTION` (L0). Profit: a saved deal instead of a refund and a lost buyer. — done 2026-11-19: options computed by code: `GET /deals/{id}/claim-options` (re-inspection, discount within the margin above the floor, replacement, partial refund, cancel) with cost to PortLess and supplier, cheapest first. Negotiating them on the threads is still the operator's.
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Document checking agent** — read what suppliers, inspectors and forwarders send (phytosanitary / origin certificates, invoices, packing lists, draft B/L, inspection reports as PDF or photo) and compare every field with the deal facts (`documents/facts.py`): names, quantities, HS code, marks, seal and container numbers, consignee, port. A mismatch → a correction request in the right thread before the B/L is final, and a compliance review. Profit: avoids customs rejections, demurrage and B/L amendment fees. — done 2026-11-19: `POST /deals/{id}/documents/check`: HS code, product, quantity (tolerance), containers, seals, buyer named / supplier never named, ports and invoice value against the deal facts; a mismatch raises DOCUMENT_ERROR. Reading PDFs / photos (OCR) is upstream.
- [x] **(Eng) P2** **Scan planning agent (where to spend the Apify budget)** — decide each day which product × market corridors to scan, re-scan or skip, from expected profit per Apify dollar (radar profit, past yield per source and corridor, price alerts, policy and news changes), within `APIFY_MAX_USD_PER_DAY`; staff see the plan and can veto. Profit: search money goes to the corridors that turn into deals. — done 2026-11-19: `GET /trade-min/scan/plan`: scan / rescan / skip per catalogue corridor by expected profit per Apify dollar, cut at the day's remaining `APIFY_MAX_USD_PER_DAY`, with a ready `scan_request`.
- [x] **(Eng) P2** **Outreach personalisation agent** — the buyer introduction is a template; let the LLM add one or two verified, company-specific lines (its product range from its website, the market fact from `outreach.market_fact`, the right language for the market), A/B-test angles per corridor, and keep the variant with the better reply rate (`funnel` + `outcomes`). Code still decides who is contacted and when. Profit: more replies from the same buyer list. — done 2026-11-19: two template openers A/B-tested per product × market (`outreach_ab.py`, `GET /deals/outreach/variants`), the better reply rate wins after `OUTREACH_AB_MIN_SENDS`; LLM company-specific lines not added (template claims only).
- [x] **(Eng) P2** **Payment chase agent** — buyers who have not funded the escrow or paid short get templated reminders today; answer their payment questions (bank charges, which account, provider steps, partial payment) from the escrow facts and agree a funding date, escalating to staff only for a refund or terms change. Profit: fewer unfunded PIs expiring. — done 2026-11-19: question agent topic `funding`: a buyer at PI_ACCEPTED / ESCROW_PENDING asking how to pay, which account, bank charges or part payment gets an answer from the escrow record (amount, provider, checkout link, charge option OUR, shortfall) behind SEND_NEGOTIATION_EMAIL. Agreeing a funding date stays open.
- [x] **(Eng) P2** **Agent scorecard** — one page per agent: actions taken, gates approved / rejected / edited, money it moved or saved (freight saved vs first quote, deals saved, reorders won), cost (LLM, Apify), and the recommended autonomy level from its own record (`/hitl-approval/learning`), so an agent earns L2 only by evidence. — done 2026-11-19: `GET /hitl-approval/scorecard?days=`: per agent gates, approved / rejected / auto / edited, money moved, agreement, recommended level (evidence only, money capped at the ceiling), platform costs.

### 23.3 Regulation and safe-market data — PortLess side of the new actors and direct feeds (2026-11-19)
Where each fact comes from, and what PortLess does with it. Actors A.29 – A.38 are in "Apify actors"; the rest are plain connectors with no Apify run. Every feed stores rows with source + date, counts in the cost meter, is cached, runs under the leader lock and has a heartbeat (stale feed → digest warning).
- [x] **(Eng) P0** **Regulation watch on A.29**: a daily job calls `trade-regulation-watch-ai` with `since` = last run, stores items (Mongo `regulatory_items`, deduplicated by hash), matches HS codes and product names against the catalogue (8-digit, synonyms from 15.1) and, for a hit, marks the HS policy entry "changed — re-confirm", holds the PI / PO on open deals of that code and pages Telegram + digest with the link (the watcher item in 14.8). `GET /deals/compliance/regulatory-items?hs=` for the desk. Until A.29 exists: a staff form to record a notification by hand with the same effect. — done 2026-11-19: `regulatory_watch.run_actor` (A.29 rows: number, type, PDF text, HS codes; `since` = last run) runs with the daily page watch; `POST /deals/compliance/regulatory-items` records a notification by hand with the same effect (re-confirm, `REGULATORY:<hs>` on open deals, Telegram); `GET /deals/compliance/regulatory-items?hs=`.
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Destination requirements from A.30 + A.31**: monthly `india-trade-portal-ai` per catalogue product × market and weekly `destination-rule-watch-ai` fill `import_requirements` (source `itp` / `eping` / regulator, date) next to the staff entries (staff always win); a changed section re-checks open prospects / deals there (`destination_requirement_changed`); the preferential duty goes into the radar's net gap and asks for the preferential certificate of origin (14.7). — done 2026-11-19: `shared/orchestration/destination_rules.py`: monthly ITP rows and weekly ePing / regulator measures stored with source and date, a changed section re-checks open deals (`DESTINATION:<cc>:<hs>`), `requirements(hs, market)` (staff first), `preferential(hs, market)` lowers the radar's duty (`_phase3_tariff_gate`) and requires the preferential certificate of origin; `GET /deals/compliance/destination-requirements`.
- [ ] **(Eng) P1** **Country profiles from direct feeds + A.32**: plain connectors for the UN consolidated list XML, OFAC sanctions programmes, EU and UK lists (country programmes only — company screening stays in `counterparty-check-ai`), the FATF "high-risk" and "increased monitoring" lists, the OECD country risk classification; A.32 for ECGC ratings, escrow providers' supported countries and attestation rules. Together they set each country's tier proposal; a compliance officer accepts a tier change (never automatic upward; a move to `blocked` applies at once) (area 24).
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Currencies of the preferred markets without a paid feed**: the ECB feed has no AED / SAR / QAR / OMR / BHD / KWD; the first five are pegged to the USD (AED 3.6725, SAR 3.75, QAR 3.64, OMR 0.3845, BHD 0.376) — set them as reference rates with source "peg" and check them monthly; KWD (basket) from the staff / bank rate. `shared/fx_rates.py` then writes to Gulf buyers in their own currency. — done 2026-11-19: `shared/fx_rates.PEGS` (AED / SAR / QAR / OMR / BHD) are reference rates with source `peg` (`FX_PEGS_ENABLED`); `check_pegs` monthly from the deal watcher pages Telegram when a recorded bank rate moved more than `FX_PEG_TOLERANCE_PCT` (0.5); KWD still needs a staff / bank rate.
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Registration checks on A.34**: PortLess's own FSSAI / RCMC / CRES numbers checked monthly (expiry into the registrations store, 14.8); a supplier's certificate numbers checked when it is added to a prospect (supplier trust, and the shipment certificates in `export_certs`). — done 2026-11-19: `shared/orchestration/registration_checks.py`: monthly lookup of PortLess's FSSAI / RCMC / CRES … (expiry updated, `source=registry`; expired / suspended / not found → Telegram); a supplier's FSSAI / APEDA numbers looked up when it is added to a prospect (`certificate_active:` / `certificate_problem:` flags).
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Refusal history on A.33 + the FDA download**: per HS × market (what to test for, e.g. ethylene oxide for spices to the EU — added to the QC booking's tests) and per supplier (a refusal in the last 24 months forces the supplier gate to L0) — closes 13.6 "Rejection history". — done 2026-11-19: `shared/orchestration/refusals.py`: A.33 rows daily + the FDA CSV (`FDA_REFUSALS_URL`, `parse_fda_csv`); `tests_for(hs, market)` adds lab tests to the QC booking note; a refusal naming the supplier in `REFUSAL_LOOKBACK_MONTHS` (24) forces `CONFIRM_SUPPLIER_SELECTION` to L0 (`supplier_import_refusal`).
- [x] **(Eng) P1** **Spend only on safe markets (A.35, A.36)**: the scan sends `countries` / `allowedCountries` from the country tiers to `export-market-finder-ai` and the worldwide `company-contact-finder-ai` search; until those inputs exist PortLess drops blocked / review markets before the run, as it already does for a prohibited product. — done 2026-11-19: the scan drops blocked / review markets (country profile) before any paid run and reports why (`SCAN_REVIEW_MARKETS` to override); the actor inputs stay with A.35 / A.36.
- [x] **(Eng) P2** **Courier tracking (A.38)**: sample and original-document AWBs polled like freight milestones; delivered → the sample step / document hand-over moves on. — done 2026-11-19: `samples.poll_couriers` from the deal watcher: shipped samples' AWBs polled (A.38 courier mode), delivered → `delivered_at` / `signed_by` on the sample. Original-document AWBs wait for a document hand-over record.
- [ ] **(QA)** Tests on recorded actor rows: a DGFT ban notification for a catalogue code holds an open deal's PI; an ITP change re-checks a prospect; a FATF listing proposes `review`; an expired FSSAI licence blocks the PI; a refused supplier goes to L0; feeds stub without a token (pinned in `tests/conftest.py`).

### 24 Many safe, low-risk markets — trade with more countries without more risk
**Today (2026-11-19).** A country is either blocked (`BLOCKED_COUNTRIES_DEFAULT`: KP, IR, SY, CU), on review (`REVIEW_COUNTRIES_DEFAULT`, 19 countries) or allowed; every allowed country is treated the same. Nothing says which markets are *good* (sure to pay, easy to ship to, escrow works there, low duty for Indian goods), so the radar can rank a hard market as high as an easy one. Freight is a regional estimate, only currencies with a fresh reference rate are used, and exposure limits are per deal / buyer / supplier / day, never per country. Goal: a wide list of safe markets that the scan, radar, outreach and money steps prefer, with the rules for each kept current.
- [ ] **(Biz/Legal)** **Choose the starter list of preferred markets** and write down why each is on it. Criteria: no sanctions and not on the FATF lists; ECGC country rating A1 / A2 (low risk of not paying); freely convertible currency with no capital controls; the buyer can fund Tazapay / Escrow.com from there; India has a trade agreement or low duty for the product; steady import demand for Indian goods. Candidates to check: UAE, Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Oman, Kuwait, Bahrain, Singapore, Malaysia, Japan, South Korea, Australia, New Zealand, UK, the EU (Netherlands, Germany, Belgium, France, Italy, Spain), USA, Canada, Mauritius. Review twice a year.
- [x] **(Eng)** **One country profile per market** instead of lists spread over the code: ISO-2, tier (`preferred` / `standard` / `review` / `blocked`), ECGC rating, FATF and sanctions status, currency and convertibility, escrow providers that accept a buyer there, trade agreement with India and its certificate of origin form, main ports (UN/LOCODE) and transit days, free days for demurrage, import requirements by product (14.7), e-mail rules, language, public holidays and time zone, each with its source and date. Mongo `country_profiles`, `GET / PUT /deals/compliance/countries` (compliance officer, audited). Compliance, landed cost, demurrage, currency and outreach read from it; the old settings stay as overrides. — done 2026-11-19: `shared/country_profiles.py` (seed for the starter markets + EU, settings lists outrank, Mongo `country_profiles`), `GET / PUT /deals/compliance/countries` (compliance officer, audited), loaded at startup.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Tier used everywhere a market is chosen.** The scan plan and the worldwide search add `preferred` markets first and propose new `standard` markets only with enough buyers; the radar shows the tier and scores the chance of closing higher for preferred markets; a `review` market needs a compliance officer before outreach (already) **and** a money approver before the PI; outreach to a market whose profile is not filled waits for it. — done 2026-11-19: scan plan (preferred first, blocked skipped), proposed markets (standard needs more buyers), radar chance ×1.1 / ×0.7 / 0, review market → `money_approver_required` on the compliance gate.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Country risk inputs refreshed on their own**, not typed once: FATF lists (updated three times a year), UN / OFAC / EU / UK sanctions country programmes, ECGC country ratings (updated every quarter), and India's own country-specific trade notices (DGFT / MEA). A change of tier re-checks open prospects and deals in that country (`country_tier_changed`, Telegram + digest); a move to `blocked` withholds every PI and money step there, as a block-level hold does. — done 2026-11-19: `COUNTRY_RISK_FEED_URL` applied daily (tier / FATF / ECGC / sanctions through the audited `put`); a tier change raises `COUNTRY:<cc>:tier_changed` on open deals + Telegram. Direct FATF / UN / OFAC connectors stay with the feeds item.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Escrow works from the buyer's country — checked before outreach.** Tazapay and Escrow.com each accept buyers from a set list of countries; today that is only found out when the buyer tries to pay. Keep each provider's country list in the profile; a buyer in a country no enabled provider serves is not contacted (or is flagged "cannot fund escrow") and the payer-country check at `escrow.funded` uses the same list. — done 2026-11-19: profile `escrow_providers`; outreach skips a buyer no enabled provider serves (`country_refusal`).
- [x] **(Eng)** **Exposure limit per country** (`EXPOSURE_MAX_COUNTRY_USD`, and a lower one for `standard` markets): open PIs + money in escrow + goods at sea per destination country, so one country's port strike, ban or currency crisis cannot hit too much of the book at once. Same approval path as the existing exposure limits. — done 2026-11-19: `EXPOSURE_MAX_COUNTRY_USD` and the lower `EXPOSURE_MAX_STANDARD_COUNTRY_USD` for non-preferred markets, same approval path.
- [x] **(Eng)** **Documents each country asks for**: certificate of origin form under the trade agreement (UAE CEPA, Australia ECTA, ASEAN, Japan, Korea, Mauritius …), attestation / legalisation of invoice and certificate of origin by chamber or embassy where needed (some Gulf markets), consular invoice, language of labels. Required per country in `export_certs` and listed in the PI so the buyer knows what it gets. — done 2026-11-19: `export_certs.country_kinds`: preferential certificate of origin, attestation, consular invoice required per destination; the PI lists the country's documents.
- [x] **(Eng)** **E-mail rules per country** before cold outreach: EU / UK (legitimate interest + opt-out, GDPR / PECR), USA (CAN-SPAM: postal address, opt-out), Canada (CASL: needs consent — no cold e-mail without it), Australia (Spam Act). Outreach checks the buyer country's rule and refuses or changes the e-mail (the Legal half is in 3.7). — done 2026-11-19: outreach waits for a profile (`COUNTRY_PROFILE_REQUIRED`), refuses consent-required markets (CASL), waits for `PORTLESS_ADDRESS` where the postal address is required (CAN-SPAM).
- [x] **(Eng)** **Freight, currency and language per preferred market**: a freight lane and transit time per main port instead of a regional estimate (16.3), a reference rate for each market's currency (AED, SAR, QAR, OMR, KWD, SGD, MYR, JPY, KRW, AUD, NZD, GBP, EUR, CAD) so the buyer sees its own currency, and the introduction's search line and opener in the market's language where buyers expect it (Arabic, Japanese, Korean). — done 2026-11-19: profile currency feeds `party_currency` (with a fresh rate), main-port transit days feed the match board, profile language the local search line.
- [ ] **(QA)** Tests: each tier through scan → outreach → PI (blocked never scanned, review needs both approvals, preferred runs through); a tier change re-checks an open deal; a buyer in a country no escrow provider serves is never contacted; country exposure limit holds the PI; one LLM journey each with a Gulf, an EU and a US buyer.


