### More facts about each company (21.2, 12)

- [ ] **(Apify) P1** A.19 **`company-contact-finder-ai` — legal-notice page (change)** — the strongest free proof that a buyer is a registered company.
  - **Source**: the Impressum / Mentions légales / Aviso legal / Note legali / Colofon / "Legal" pages that EU (and many Gulf) company sites must publish.
  - **Row**: `legalNotice { legalName, legalForm (GmbH / SARL / BV / LLC …), registerCourt, registerNumber (e.g. HRB 12345), vatId, managingDirectors[], registeredAddress, shareCapital, sourceUrl, language }`.
  - **Rules**: parse per language with fixed labels ("Registergericht", "Handelsregister", "RCS", "KvK", "P.IVA"). Keep the raw text block in `legalNotice.rawText` (≤ 2,000 characters).
  - **Done when**: 20 German / French / Dutch buyer sites give a register number where the page has one.
  - **PortLess side**: 21.2 "legal notice" (VAT → VIES, register number → A.25, legal name on the deal party).
- [ ] **(Apify) P1** A.20 **`company-contact-finder-ai` — search in other languages (change)**
  - **Why**: PortLess now sends one local-language line per market (`shared/search_terms.py`). The actor must search it properly.
  - **Input**: `queries[]` may be non-English and non-Latin (Arabic, Turkish, Chinese, Japanese); optional `googleDomain` / `hl` per line (else derived from the line's country: `google.de` / `hl=de`, `google.ae` / `hl=ar`).
  - **Row / OUTPUT**: `query`, `queryLanguage`, `googleDomain` on each row and in OUTPUT `queries[]`.
  - **Rules**: names in non-Latin script are kept as written plus a `nameLatin` transliteration.
  - **Done when**: an Arabic line for AE returns UAE companies, with the language reported.
  - **PortLess side**: none beyond reading `queryLanguage` into the scan report.
- [ ] **(Apify) P2** A.21 **`company-contact-finder-ai` — every phone, typed (change)**
  - **Row**: `phones[] { number (E.164), type (mobile | landline | tollfree | unknown), whatsapp (bool — the site links wa.me / api.whatsapp.com for that number), label (sales / export / office as written), sourceUrl }`; `phone` stays the best one.
  - **PortLess side**: phone check + WhatsApp relay (`shared/phone_check.py`) on every number.
- [ ] **(Apify) P2** A.22 **`company-contact-finder-ai` — mailbox status per address (change)**
  - **Row**: with `verifyMailbox` on, `emails[] { email, mailbox (deliverable | undeliverable | catch_all | unknown), role (bool, e.g. info@), sourceUrl }` for every address, not only `bestEmail`.
