### Regulations and safe markets (3.1, 14.7, 14.8, 24 — added 2026-11-19)

Rule for actor or not: an actor only where the source is a web page with no API or download (DGFT, CBIC, India Trade Portal, ECGC, FoSCoS, the commodity boards, Ministry of Textiles). Where an official file or API exists, PortLess reads it directly with a plain connector, which is cheaper and needs no Apify run: UN / OFAC / EU / UK sanctions lists, the FATF lists page, the OECD country risk table, WTO tariff data, ECB rates, US FDA import refusal data. The PortLess side of each actor is in 23.3.

- [ ] **(Apify) P0** A.29 **`trade-regulation-watch-ai` (new)** — every new Indian export rule, the day it is published.
  - **Why**: one missed ban or minimum export price can make a whole container illegal to ship. Replaces the manual weekly review (3.1). PortLess's `regulatory_watch` today reads only the list pages' text.
  - **Source**: DGFT notifications, public notices and trade notices; CBIC customs notifications (tariff and non-tariff, export duty); APEDA, Spices Board, MPEDA and FSSAI circulars; Ministry of Textiles notifications (RoSCTL rates); the RoDTEP schedule (Appendix 4R) changes.
  - **Input**: `since` (date of the last run), `sources[]` (default all).
  - **Row**: `source`, `number`, `date`, `title`, `type` (`prohibition` | `restriction` | `minimum_export_price` | `export_duty` | `incentive_rate` | `procedure` | `other`), `pdfUrl`, `pdfText` (trimmed), `hsCodes[]` (ITC-HS / CTH codes found in the text, 4–8 digits), `products[]` (product names found), `effectiveFrom`, `textHash`.
  - **Rules**: output only items newer than `since` (by number + date). PDF text is extracted from scanned PDFs too (OCR only when there is no text layer). Hindi-only notices keep the Hindi title plus an English title when one is published.
  - **Done when**: the last 30 days of DGFT notifications are all listed, with HS codes found in a ban notice.
  - **PortLess side**: 23.3 "Regulation watch on A.29".
- [ ] **(Apify) P1** A.30 **`india-trade-portal-ai` (new)** — what the importing country asks of an Indian product.
  - **Source**: indiantradeportal.in per ITC-HS code × importing country. Check the site's terms first (some pages need a free sign-in).
  - **Input**: `hsCodes[]`, `countries[]`.
  - **Row** (one per HS × country): `mfnTariffPct`, `preferentialTariffs[] { agreement, ratePct, rulesOfOrigin }`, `spsMeasures[]`, `tbtMeasures[]`, `otherNtm[]`, `importLicensing`, `borderDocuments[]`, `pageUrl`, `readOn`, `sectionHashes { tariff, sps, tbt, documents }`.
  - **Rules**: a section that changed since the last run is flagged `changed_sections[]`. Cache a month.
  - **PortLess side**: 23.3 "Destination requirements from A.30 + A.31".
- [ ] **(Apify) P1** A.31 **`destination-rule-watch-ai` (new)** — rule changes on the importing side.
  - **Source**: WTO ePing SPS / TBT notifications by country and product (new limits, bans, labelling, certificates); the rule pages of the main preferred-market regulators: EU food and feed rules, US FDA import alerts, SFDA (Saudi), UAE MOCCAE / Dubai Municipality, Japan MHLW, FSANZ.
  - **Input**: `countries[]`, `hsCodes[]`, `since`.
  - **Row**: `country`, `regulator`, `hsCodes[]`, `products[]`, `measure` (text), `measureType` (`mrl` | `ban` | `labelling` | `certificate` | `testing` | `other`), `publishedOn`, `inForceFrom`, `commentDeadline`, `link`.
  - **Rules**: runs weekly.
  - **PortLess side**: 23.3 (catalogue `import_requirements` re-checked; open deals to that market get a review finding).
- [ ] **(Apify) P1** A.32 **`country-risk-feed-ai` (new)** — the country facts that are only web pages, including the **ECGC country categories A1 … D**.
  - **Source**: ECGC country risk classification (A1, A2, B1, B2, C1, C2, D — published quarterly), India's country-specific trade notices (DGFT / MEA), the escrow providers' supported-country pages (Tazapay, Escrow.com), and embassy / chamber attestation rules for invoices and certificates of origin (Gulf markets).
