  - **PortLess side**: compliance findings from the one result; no second run.
- [ ] **(Apify) P2** A.38 **`multi-carrier-tracking-ai` (with A.27) — courier AWBs for samples and original documents (change)**
  - **Source**: public tracking pages of DHL Express, FedEx, Aramex, UPS and India Post Speed Post.
  - **Input**: `trackingNumbers[]` lines "AWB, courier".
  - **Row**: `trackingNumber`, `courier`, `status` (`picked_up` | `in_transit` | `customs` | `out_for_delivery` | `delivered` | `exception`), `lastScan`, `lastScanAt`, `deliveredAt`, `signedBy`.
  - **PortLess side**: 23.3 "Courier tracking (A.38)" (samples step, original B/L / certificate-of-origin courier).

### New from the 2026-11-19 term check

- [ ] **(Apify) P1** A.39 **`trade-map-ai` (new — only if ITC's terms allow automated reading; otherwise staff import the Trade Map exports, see 17.1)** — ITC Trade Map data that Comtrade lacks.
  - **Why**: monthly / quarterly figures for many reporters, mirror data for markets that report late (Gulf, Africa), unit values per partner, India's competitors per market, and lists of importing companies by product and country.
  - **Source**: trademap.org (ITC; free registration, free for users in developing countries such as India). Uses PortLess's own account.
  - **Input**: `hsCodes[]` (6 digits; national 8 / 10 where shown), `countries[]`, `view` (`imports_by_partner` | `monthly` | `companies`), `periods`.
  - **Row** (trade): `reporter`, `partner`, `hsCode`, `period`, `valueUsd`, `quantity`, `unit`, `unitValueUsdPerMt`, `mirror` (bool). Row (companies): `companyName`, `country`, `city`, `website`, `products[]`, `role` (importer / exporter), `employees`.
  - **PortLess side**: 17.1 "ITC Trade Map as a source".
- [ ] **(Apify) P2** A.40 **`customs-broker-directory-ai` (new)** — licensed customs brokers (CHA) per port.
  - **Why**: to choose and check the CHA for each port (5.2 "CHA hand-off"). A broker's licence must be valid under CBLR 2018.
  - **Source**: CBIC / customs commissionerates' published lists of licensed customs brokers (PDF / HTML per zone), plus the brokers' own sites for contact details.
  - **Input**: `ports[]` (UN/LOCODE or customs port code, e.g. INNSA1), `zones[]`.
  - **Row**: `firmName`, `licenceNumber`, `licenceValidUntil`, `commissionerate`, `ports[]`, `address`, `phone`, `email`, `website`, `listPublishedOn`.
  - **PortLess side**: seed for `cha_agents` (5.2), licence validity checked before each hand-off.

